  "worked_solution": "The modes of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that the global maxima of $f(x)$ are at $x=1,5,10.$\n\nTherefore, the modes of $X$ are $1,5$ and $10.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/d82edc89a519c6286f665c217871965b889697e87c3a4d6176f2e29e8b7596ac.png)",
